"answer": "Project Zenith is a data analytics initiative led by Sarah Tan, with an initial budget of $500,000 (later adjusted to $550,000) and a kick-off scheduled for June 15th. The project has progressed through several phases, including design, development (led by Omar Jensen), and testing, with a prototype for secure file sharing successfully tested ahead of schedule. Strategic partnerships have been established with TechInnovate, and the team has expanded with five new members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture, joining in an onboarding session on September 10th. Recent milestones include the completion of the testing phase, celebrated on October 10th, and upcoming plans for user interface enhancements in October. Security protocols, including multi-factor authentication and encryption, are being updated effective January next year. The project is currently seeking stakeholder feedback on the prototype by the end of November, with a final phase confirmation requested by the end of the week."
